        "original_id": "05583938-b333-5473-a0ea-51f03e475037",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: KSPN-FM\n- People: David Byrne, Shane Shu, Tom Petty, Van Morrison, Ben Harper, Stephen Thomas Erlewine, David Bowie, Robert Plant, Prince\n- Bands: Talking Heads, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, Widespread Panic\n- Music formats and genres: AAA format, classic rock, new wave, punk, art rock, funk, world music\n- Places: New York City\n\nFacts:\n- Talking Heads were an American rock band formed in 1975 in New York City and active until 1991.\n- David Byrne, born on 14 May 1952, is a Scottish-born American musician who was the founding member, principal songwriter, lead singer, and guitarist of Talking Heads.\n- Talking Heads helped pioneer new wave music by integrating punk, art rock, funk, and world music with avant-garde sensibilities and an anxious, clean-cut image.\n- Critic Stephen Thomas Erlewine described Talking Heads as one of the most critically acclaimed bands of the 1980s.\n- KSPN-FM features the AAA format, combining classic rock hits by Tom Petty, Van Morrison, and Talking Heads with newer musicians such as Ben Harper, Blues Traveler, Sonia Dada, and Widespread Panic.\n- Shane Shu's mezzo-soprano voice has been compared to David Bowie, David Byrne, and Robert Plant, and his dress sense has been compared to Prince.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
